Feature: Complete only the accepted feature scope
  Execution verifies the admitted plan; future improvements belong to planning.

  Scenario: Complementary evidence satisfies the accepted feature
    Given browser journeys and component alternatives are the accepted approach
    And their native automated execution reports pass
    And the user separately acknowledges manual test execution
    And the parent EPIC contains unrelated future criteria
    When completion readiness assesses the current feature baseline
    Then the accepted criteria are satisfied collectively
    And no additional browser-only scenario or parent criterion blocks completion
    And no coverage-link confirmation is required
    And useful extra verification is recorded as a future planning proposal

  Scenario: A real accepted assertion is missing
    Given an accepted criterion requires saving and reopening a form
    And existing assertions only verify saving
    When readiness assesses the inspected assertion sources
    Then it records the exact unmet accepted obligation
    And the phase fixer receives that obligation and preserves passing proof
    And subsequent refreshes cannot replace this finding with a generic execution request

  Scenario: Missing context is recovered without inventing missing code
    Given a selected test delegates its assertion to an admitted repository helper
    When assessment requests the missing helper
    Then HEPHA retrieves the helper within admitted source roots
    And reassesses the same criteria without changing tests or manual results
    And unavailable context remains a verification issue with a readiness retry action

  Scenario: Future advice does not stale completed verification
    Given the current feature has passing tests and completed human checkpoints
    When HEPHA publishes an additional improvement proposal
    Then the accepted baseline remains unchanged
    And fresh execution and saved human results remain applicable
    And the feature is ready for the explicit Complete Feature action

  Scenario: Manual acknowledgement is separate from automated coverage
    Given automated assertions and reports satisfy the accepted criteria
    And manual test execution has not been acknowledged
    When readiness assesses the feature
    Then automated acceptance coverage is satisfied
    And only the independent human acknowledgement remains pending
    When the user acknowledges manual test execution
    Then completion becomes available without reassessing unchanged automated evidence

  Scenario: Manual links cannot establish automated acceptance
    Given a manual case has a recorded user PASS
    When an assessment uses that manual case as an acceptance contribution
    Then the automated-only response contract rejects the contribution
    And the model must correct the link using automated test evidence

  Scenario: Manual documents do not become automated obligations
    Given the admitted plan includes an explicit manual-only qualification
    When readiness builds the automated acceptance scope
    Then the manual-only qualification is excluded without inventing an automated replacement
    And changing manual cases or results does not invalidate automated assessment evidence

  Scenario: Shared assertions require more than two retrieval hops
    Given a passing automated test delegates through three source helpers
    When each assessment requests the next missing helper
    Then every subsequent assessment retains all previously retrieved bodies
    And retrieval continues while new source is available within the context budget
    And the accepted criterion is resolved from the collective assertions
    And no test execution or manual acknowledgement is repeated

  Scenario: Pending evidence does not reopen satisfied criteria
    Given one accepted criterion is satisfied and another needs a shared helper
    When HEPHA retrieves the shared helper
    Then only the pending criterion is requested in the next assessment
    And both validated criterion decisions are retained in the final result

  Scenario: Feature document references include section and line locations
    Given the feature folder is admitted separately from the source repository
    When assessment cites a feature section anchor or phase task location
    Then HEPHA retrieves that document inside the admitted feature folder
    And source line ranges resolve to their complete assertion file
    And unadmitted paths remain inaccessible

  Scenario: Repeated source requests cannot manufacture coverage
    Given an assessment still cannot establish an accepted obligation after retrieval
    When it requests the same inspected reference again
    Then retrieval stops without another identical assessment call
    And the criterion remains evidence pending rather than passed or missing implementation
